 "renames": {
  "NLAlib/Matrix/Cholesky.lean": "collides with existing NLAlib/Matrix/Factorizations/Cholesky.lean (the IsCholesky/recursion file); this one is the complete `cholesky_decomposition` contract importing the CholeskyCharacterization chain, so it is named like the other *Toolkit contract files"
 },
 "notes": [
  "M7a covers the 122 codex content files NLAlib/Matrix/[A-H]*.lean; Basic.lean, Calculus.lean, Factorizations.lean, Functions.lean in NLAlib/Matrix/ are generated aggregators and are not mapped.",
  "No file in the range imports anything outside NLAlib.Matrix/NLAlib.ForMathlib or any Mathlib Probability/MeasureTheory module, so all stay in layer 0.",
  "Families kept together: Cholesky* + ComplexCholeskyPivot -> Factorizations; CS*/CanonicalCS/ComplexCS* + ComplexOblique*/ComplexIdempotentRealForm/ComplexFrameTransport + GramIsometry/ComplexGramIsometry -> Subspaces (CS decomposition as the principal-angle canonical form; CSToolkit bundles the oblique-projection contract, so Subspaces avoids splitting it; ObliqueProjection*/PrincipalAngle* from M7b should land in Subspaces too); DavisKahan* + CoupledNormBounds/GoldenRatioBlock (Wedin engines) -> Perturbation; Hadamard* (Schur product) + FiniteExponentialGram, Block* (PSD block contraction), determinant inequalities (Hadamard/Fischer/Szasz/Minkowski/log-det), Horn product and Hermitian-part majorization -> Inequalities; Diagonalizable*, EigenvectorPairing/Deflation*, GeneralizedEigen*, AdjugateRankOne, CharpolySimplicity, Gershgorin*/DiagonalDominance*, definite congruence -> Spectral.",
  "Eigenvalue* is split by content: EigenvalueOrder/EigenvalueEquality/EigenvalueSimplicity/Eigenframes/EigenframeDecomposition -> Spectral; the atlas `eigenvalue-perturbation-symmetric` and `eigenvalue-residual-bounds` families (EigenvaluePerturbation*, EigenvalueTrace, EigenvaluePencil, EigenvalueVariation, EigenvalueResidualToolkit, EigenspaceProjector) plus BauerFike*, HoffmanWielandtNormal -> Perturbation (next to SpectralContinuity).",
  "ConditionNumber/ConditionNumberToolkit/DistanceToSingularity -> Perturbation next to the existing Conditioning.lean."
 ],
 "flags": [
  "NLAlib/Matrix/ComplexCholeskyPivot.lean: the real content; NLAlib/LowRank/Cholesky/ComplexCholeskyPivot.lean is a declaration-free compatibility shim that only imports it (same base name, different directory, so no collision). Placed in Matrix/Factorizations because CholeskyTrailingResidual imports it; the shim can be deleted later.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/GramColumnExchange.lean: Gu-Eisenstat maximum-volume column exchange identity; placed in Factorizations to sit with the RRQR family (MaximumVolume*, StrongRankRevealingQR, RankRevealing* in M7b) -- M7b should place those in Factorizations too, or move this file with them.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/BlockNormBounds.lean: generic block spectral/Frobenius bounds (supports strong RRQR constants); placed in Norms.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/FanDominance.lean: Fan dominance for invariant norms plus a Mirsky invariant-norm perturbation consequence; placed in Norms with the InvariantNorm*/SymmetricGauge family (M7b); the Mirsky part could later split to Perturbation.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/EigenspaceProjector.lean: defines eigenspace projectors via CFC (Spectral material) but most content is residual sine bounds; placed in Perturbation with EigenvalueResidualToolkit (ResidualBounds/RayleighDerivative in M7b should follow).",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/EigenvaluePencil.lean, EigenvalueVariation.lean: eigenvalue continuity/first-variation lemmas supporting Lidskii; placed in Perturbation. If M7b puts Lidskii* in Inequalities these could follow it.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/ComplexQZ.lean: generalized Schur (QZ) triangularisation of pencils; placed in Spectral following the Schur-triangularisation hint. RealQZ/RealPencilTriangularization (M7b) should go to the same leaf.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/DeterminantDerivative.lean, DeterminantDerivativeFinite.lean: Jacobi's formula; placed in Calculus (the derivative leaf) rather than Basic.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/GeneralizedSchurComplement.lean: Moore-Penrose generalized Schur complement with PSD criteria and order bounds; placed in Basic next to SchurComplement.lean (it imports MoorePenroseTransformations, which M7b should also place low, e.g. Basic).",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/ComplexDiagonalMajorization.lean, HermitianPart*.lean: Schur-Horn type majorization statements; placed in Inequalities on the assumption that Majorization*/SchurHorn* (M7b) go to Inequalities -- keep consistent."
 ]
}